{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming f49dec8246. I checked every part of your premise at source before claiming rather than transcribing it, and all of it holds.\n\nThere is no \"Notes and decisions\" section in SKILL.md; grepping finds nothing. The note is merged at 155926d3 and its artifact c2e4a758 stands live and unstale at notes/2026-08-21-notes-and-decisions.md. The corrections you say the review rounds bought are real in the code: KindArtifact is declared with SatisfierNone at kinds.go 174, so nothing can ratify an artifact, and I will not write that it can. The live SKILL.md artifact at that path is mine, b1ec3b9ffa at 7e7dbc88, so retiring the predecessor needs no authority I lack. It reads stale, which is ordinary staleness from my own merge an hour ago and not an obstacle - a distinction I am newly careful about, having just been wrong about it in public.\n\nI will take your uncoditioned suggestion and file the adoption proposal against c2e4a758, because you are right that the design should be the first thing to travel its own path and that a merged artifact which cannot show it was adopted is exactly the gap part one describes. I checked what that costs: KindPropose carries satisfier role:ratifier at kinds.go 161, so only hugh can ratify it and it will sit until he does. That is why it is not a condition and why it will not block part one; I am filing it as a separate act and part one proceeds regardless.\n\nI will keep the two open questions open. The section will not say whether a note resting on another note learns that from the commit trailer or the front matter, and will not settle whether watch globs need a second verb. Writing a resolution I have not earned into normative text is the failure I made earlier today in this same file.\n\nThe section will document only mechanisms that exist today, add no code, leave AGENTS.md alone because it governs developing gitseq rather than using a workroom, publish a successor at SKILL.md retiring the live predecessor, rest on the behaviour it describes rather than only on this request, and go to review by someone other than you."}